00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:36.070
MARK MANDEL: We have
statistical representation

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:37.180
of people having a good time.

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:37.360
JOHN BROWN: Yes.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.049
We have data.

00:12:38.049 --> 00:12:39.090
We have data on that now.

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:40.740
FRANCESC CAMPOY: That is
a good problem to have.

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:41.830
That is a good skew to have.

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:42.580
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:43.520
Yeah, definitely.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:44.000
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
That is awesome.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.510
Well, thank you so much, again,
John, for taking the time

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:47.569
to talk with us.

00:12:47.569 --> 00:12:48.860
We know you're very busy today.

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:50.140
JOHN BROWN: Yeah I'm
gonna go back over there.

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:50.520
MARK MANDEL: Wonderful.

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:51.370
Thank you so much.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.130
JOHN BROWN: Thank you two.

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:52.533
FRANCESC CAMPOY: See you later.

00:12:52.533 --> 00:12:53.340
JOHN BROWN: Bye.

